    {
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -260,
        -60
      ],
      "size": [
        580,
        720
      ],
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "OmniCam -> MiniMax H3 native  (profile: h3_native)\n\nBase template: Comfy-Org/workflow_templates\n  video_minimax_h3_r2v.json\nUNet, Qwen3-VL text encoder, both VAEs, res_multistep / simple and the\noptional 4-step turbo LoRA are unchanged from it.\n\nWHAT CHANGED\nThe playblast becomes the motion reference: Monitor.reference_frames feeds\nref_video_0 as IMAGE frames at 24 fps, which is the transport this node\nexpects. The template's ComfyMathExpression that computed 17n+5 is gone -\nMonitor resolves the aligned length itself and drives it.\n\nThe prompt now comes from Monitor.final_prompt: your base prompt plus a\ncamera-motion fragment that tells the model to copy the move and NOT the\nproxy's grey-box appearance. Edit base_prompt on the Monitor, not here.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Author the shot in the Director and click Playblast. This one needs it.\n2. Keep the LoadImage nodes for subject identity (<Picture 1>, <Picture 2>).\n3. Queue.\n\nLENGTH AND DURATION\nH3 needs 17n+5 frames at 24 fps. 5.0s = 120 frames, resolved up to 124.\nThe reference itself must be 2-15s; preflight checks the connected\nplayblast and warns outside that window.\n\nMULTI-SHOT IS ALLOWED HERE\nCut between cameras and the playblast carries the cuts frame for frame.\nMonitor then drops the single-camera prompt for a neutral one, because no\none trajectory describes an edit.\n\nMODELS REQUIRED\n  diffusion_models/minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors\n  text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors\n  vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors\n  vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors\n  loras/minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_4step_v0.1_comfyui_bf16.safetensors (optional)"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "id": 149,
      "flags": {},
      "mode": 0,
      "order": 28,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": []
    }
